<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John V, Duke of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1389">1389</a>–<a href="/years/1442">1442</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John V was duke of Brittany from 1399 to 1442, the son of John IV. He kept Brittany largely out of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, shifting between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and survived his kidnapping by the rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penthievre">Penthièvre</a> family in 1420. His long reign brought prosperity, building and administrative development to the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-v-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="John V, Duke of Brittany" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dom Hyacinthe Morice · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Jean_V_-_Duc_de_Bretagne.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
